.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NQCHKT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqchkt
.Nd check a capsule and its RFC 3161 timestamp
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqchkt
.Fa "const char *dir"
.Fa "const uint8_t *trust" "size_t trustlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *const *anc" "const size_t *anclen" "size_t nanc"
.Fa "nqrep **rep"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqchkt
is
.Xr nqchk 3
with
.Fa nanc
trust anchors for time-stamping authorities (TSAs):
.Fa anc Ns Bq i
is a DER X.509 certificate of
.Fa anclen Ns Bq i
bytes, for i below
.Fa nanc ,
at most 32.
.Pp
With anchors, the seal must carry a
.Ql timestamp :
the base64 of an RFC 3161 time-stamp token.
The
.Ql timestamp
row passes only when
.Bl -bullet
.It
the token parses as a strict DER RFC 3161 token;
.It
its message imprint is its own hash (SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512) of the
decoded
.Ql signature
bytes of the seal;
.It
its signature verifies under the TSA's certificate, whose path leads to
one of the anchors and is valid at the token's genTime;
.El
and the row's detail then gives the genTime.
A seal without a timestamp fails the row.
.Pp
With
.Fa nanc
0,
.Fn nqchkt
is exactly
.Fn nqchk :
a timestamp present fails its row
.Pq Dq not checked: no TSA trust anchors given ,
and no timestamp gives no row.
.Pp
The timestamp proves that the signature existed at genTime, according to
the TSA.
It does not make an untrusted seal key trusted; pin the key with
.Fa trust .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
As for
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
and also:
.Bl -tag -width NQELIM
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fa nanc
is over 32.
No report.
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa nanc
is nonzero and
.Fa anc
or
.Fa anclen
is
.Dv NULL ,
or an anchor is
.Dv NULL
or empty.
No report.
An anchor that is not a certificate fails the
.Ql timestamp
row instead.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
const uint8_t *anc[1] = {tsa_der};
size_t anclen[1] = {tsa_der_len};
nqrep *rep = NULL;
int rc = nqchkt("results", pk, sizeof pk, anc, anclen, 1, &rep);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqrep 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 3161
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)
.%D August 2001
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 5280
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate and CRL Profile
.%D May 2008
.Re
.Sh CAVEATS
Neither the library nor
.Xr noqtis-seal 1
can yet obtain a timestamp, and
.Xr noqtis-check 1
takes no anchors; timestamps are checked only through this function.
